<title>USA: Tuscarora sets 3-for-2 split.</title>
<headline>Tuscarora sets 3-for-2 split.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRIGHTON, Pa. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuscarora Inc said Wednesday its board had declared a three-for-two stock split, payable about January 11, record December 27.</p>
<p>Cash will be paid in lieu of fractional shares, it said.</p>
<p>John O'Leary Jr, president and chief executive officer, said in a statement the split will increase the number of shares outstanding from 6.3 million to 9.4 million.</p>
<p>The stock distribution was declared to enhance shareholder value, he said. &quot;By increasing the number of shares available, we anticipate increased trading volume and improved liquidity for the company's stock,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
